monopoly.description:
Monopoly is an independent multiplayer economic board-game experience built as a Telegram Mini App. It started as my graduation project and evolved into a live product with real users, multiplayer matches, a managed game economy, monetization, analytics, customer support and a dedicated administration system. The project is independent and is not presented as an official product of the Monopoly trademark owner.

My role:
- created the original product concept and defined the complete user journey;
- worked as Product Lead, Team Lead and Lead Frontend Developer;
- designed the game rules, modes, room structure, progression and economic model;
- owned the complete frontend implementation and coordinated backend and design delivery;
- prepared the roadmap, priorities, technical tasks, API requirements and release scope;
- analyzed player behavior and used product data to improve onboarding, retention and monetization.

Product and gameplay:
- built game discovery, room creation, matchmaking, invitations and multiplayer sessions;
- implemented the game board, turn flow, player cards, events, contextual actions and match recovery scenarios;
- created player profiles, statistics, inventories, friends, quests, notifications and trade offers;
- developed the item shop, player marketplace, listings, exchanges, cases, keys and VIP features;
- designed guided onboarding and an interactive tutorial that teaches complex rules directly on the board.

Frontend and Telegram experience:
- developed the complete responsive client for Telegram WebView on iOS, Android and desktop;
- adapted dense board-game information to both compact mobile screens and wide desktop layouts;
- handled safe areas, embedded navigation, responsive states, modal flows and reconnect scenarios;
- translated product requirements and design concepts into reusable screens, component states and working interactions;
- kept the path from opening the Mini App to joining the first match short and understandable.

Economy and monetization:
- designed the circulation of in-game currency, Telegram Stars, item rarity, rewards and marketplace fees;
- defined cases, keys, gifts, VIP benefits, sponsored quests and paid digital goods;
- balanced currency sources and sinks to reduce uncontrolled inflation;
- evaluated how prices, rewards and fees influence trading, session activity, retention and potential revenue;
- designed monetization around convenience, collection and expanded experience rather than direct pay-to-win mechanics.

Team leadership, backend and operations:
- decomposed product features and coordinated frontend, backend and design work;
- specified room states, turns, match events, reconnect behavior, payments, inventory, trading and support flows;
- designed an administration area for users, matches, content, support tickets, broadcasts, surveys and product metrics;
- added audience segmentation for VIP status, match activity, purchases, payment totals and inactivity;
- incorporated financial tracking, monetization data and administrative action history into the operational model.

The result is not a visual prototype but a complex game product spanning product strategy, frontend engineering, multiplayer interaction, game economy, team leadership and ongoing data-informed development.

lavanda.description:
Lavanda is a responsive e-commerce showcase and content management platform for a lavender farm and natural-products brand. I designed and implemented the Next.js frontend, customer purchase flows and protected administration area, combining a visually rich storefront with editable content and direct customer communication.

Storefront and customer journey:
- built the homepage around the brand story, lavender production, product catalog, purchasing information, delivery, field visits and contacts;
- created a responsive visual system with lavender tones, editorial typography and reusable sections for desktop, tablet and mobile;
- developed a dynamic catalog with categories, featured products, badges, product details and empty states;
